    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/43095492-e3cf-4cb8-841d-93a31f614c0f-1.png\" style=\"width: 170px; height: 187px;\" /></p><p>Bromine undergo <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> hybridization and the shape of the molecule is T-shape. Each fluorine is having <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> lone pairs and bromine is having <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> lone pairs. Hence, total <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn></math> lone pairs are there.</p>",
